### 8: Database Schema Creation

The database schema was designed to efficiently store and manage the project data related to microplastic detection. The schema includes tables for user information, sensor details, detection records, sample information, and system logs. Proper relationships between the tables were established to maintain data integrity and support future system expansion.

### 9: UI Wireframe Design

Basic wireframes were created to visualize the structure and workflow of the application. The wireframes included layouts for the login page, dashboard, navigation panel, data entry forms, and result display screens. These designs served as a blueprint for the user interface development process.

### 10: Login & Dashboard UI Design

The user interface for the login page and dashboard was designed using modern design principles. The login page provides secure user authentication, while the dashboard offers an overview of sensor status, microplastic detection results, recent activities, and important system metrics in a user-friendly manner.

### 11: Navigation & Form Design

Navigation menus and data input forms were designed to improve accessibility and ease of use. The navigation structure enables users to move smoothly between different sections of the application. Forms were developed to collect sample details, sensor readings, and user inputs efficiently with proper validation considerations.

### 12: Design Review

A detailed review of the proposed designs was conducted to evaluate functionality, usability, and consistency. Feedback was gathered and necessary modifications were identified to enhance the overall user experience and ensure that the design aligns with the project objectives and requirements.

### 13: Frontend Environment Setup

The frontend development environment was successfully configured by installing the necessary tools, frameworks, libraries, and dependencies. The project structure was organized, version control support was established, and the environment was prepared for the implementation of the application interface.





